  "biography": {
    "plain_text": "Sir Nigel Broackes was a British property developer who founded Trafalgar House. After early ventures consumed much of an inheritance, a London flat-conversion project provided the basis for his business. Working with Victor Matthews, he developed the group into a diversified enterprise whose interests included the Cunard shipping line, the Ritz and newspapers.",
